{"id":"h07t3","name":"Daily Consumption with Meter Resets","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The table <b>readings</b> has the columns <code>meter_id</code>, <code>read_at</code> (timestamp) and <code>counter</code> (numeric, kWh). The counter of a meter is cumulative: the consumption between two readings is the difference between the two counters.</p>\n<p>The data has three problems:</p>\n<ul><li>The same reading can be sent several times: for a meter and a <code>read_at</code>, keep only the highest counter.</li>\n<li>When a meter is replaced, its counter restarts from 0. When a counter is lower than the previous one, the consumption of that interval is the new counter itself (counted from 0).</li>\n<li>The first reading of a meter has no previous value: its consumption is 0.</li></ul>\n<p>The consumption of an interval belongs to the day (date) of its later reading. For each meter and each day with at least one reading, compute <code>kwh</code> (total consumption of the day, rounded to 1 decimal) and <code>readings</code> (number of distinct reading times that day). A day is flagged <code>'SPIKE'</code> when its unrounded consumption is more than 3 times the average daily consumption of that meter (average over the days listed for that meter), else <code>'OK'</code>.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the columns <code>meter_id</code>, <code>day</code>, <code>kwh</code>, <code>readings</code> and <code>flag</code>, sorted by <code>meter_id</code>, then <code>day</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>readings</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>meter_id</th><th>read_at</th><th>counter</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 08:00:00</td><td>100.0</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 18:00:00</td><td>104.5</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02 18:00:00</td><td>104.0</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-03 09:00:00</td><td>110.0</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-03 10:40:00</td><td>2.5</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-04 10:00:00</td><td>6.0</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-05 09:20:00</td><td>40.0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 09:00:00</td><td>50.0</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>meter_id</th><th>day</th><th>kwh</th><th>readings</th><th>flag</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>4.5</td><td>2</td><td>OK</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-03</td><td>8.0</td><td>2</td><td>OK</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-04</td><td>3.5</td><td>1</td><td>OK</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2026-03-05</td><td>34.0</td><td>1</td><td>OK</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02</td><td>0.0</td><td>1</td><td>OK</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> tables <code>readings</code><br><b>[output]</b> the result of one query with exactly the columns <code>meter_id</code>, <code>day</code>, <code>kwh</code>, <code>readings</code>, <code>flag</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["compteurs cumulés","remise à zéro","doublons","LAG","moyenne par fenêtre"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>query.sql</code>. Efface le commentaire de départ si tu veux.</li><li>Écris <b>une seule requête</b> qui commence par <code>SELECT</code> (ou <code>WITH</code>). Les tables <code>readings</code> existent déjà, remplies avec les données du test : pas de <code>CREATE TABLE</code> ni d'<code>INSERT</code>.</li><li>Le moteur est PostgreSQL. Si tu écris plusieurs requêtes, seul le résultat de la dernière est noté.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Le résultat de ta requête doit avoir <b>exactement 5 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>meter_id</code>, <code>day</code>, <code>kwh</code>, <code>readings</code>, <code>flag</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Nomme chaque colonne calculée avec <code>AS</code>.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>ORDER BY</code> à la fin de la requête).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé ; les dates s'affichent AAAA-MM-JJ.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 8 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"readings":{"columns":[["meter_id","INT"],["read_at","TIMESTAMP"],["counter","NUMERIC(10,1)"]],"rows":[[1,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",100.0],[1,"2026-03-02 18:00:00",104.5],[1,"2026-03-02 18:00:00",104.0],[1,"2026-03-03 09:00:00",110.0],[1,"2026-03-03 10:40:00",2.5],[1,"2026-03-04 10:00:00",6.0],[1,"2026-03-05 09:20:00",40.0],[2,"2026-03-02 09:00:00",50.0]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["meter_id","day","kwh","readings","flag"],"rows":[[1,"2026-03-02",4.5,2,"OK"],[1,"2026-03-03",8.0,2,"OK"],[1,"2026-03-04",3.5,1,"OK"],[1,"2026-03-05",34.0,1,"OK"],[2,"2026-03-02",0.0,1,"OK"]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"readings":{"columns":[["meter_id","INT"],["read_at","TIMESTAMP"],["counter","NUMERIC(10,1)"]],"rows":[[3,"2026-03-02 08:00:00",0.0],[3,"2026-03-03 08:00:00",1.0],[3,"2026-03-04 08:00:00",2.0],[3,"2026-03-05 08:00:00",3.0],[3,"2026-03-06 08:00:00",30.0]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["meter_id","day","kwh","readings","flag"],"rows":[[3,"2026-03-02",0.0,1,"OK"],[3,"2026-03-03",1.0,1,"OK"],[3,"2026-03-04",1.0,1,"OK"],[3,"2026-03-05",1.0,1,"OK"],[3,"2026-03-06",27.0,1,"SPIKE"]]}}],"hidden_n":8,"hidden":"","solution":""}